SRC/jumble2 -- Dan Heller's jumble game, as built for OS-9/68000================================================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.games carried it.  jumble.c differs fromit only inside #ifdef OSK:  - the word list is /dd/GAMES/words, which this disk already carries, and    the high scores live in /dd/GAMES/JUMBLE2/scores.  The game opens that    file for update, so it ships, empty.  - SIGALRM is 5, the number unix.l's alarm() sends; OS-9's signal.h names    none.  Measured: with one word at expert level, `Time ran out.' appears    when the 91 seconds are up, while the game is waiting for a guess.  - random() and srandom() are rand() and srand(), from /dd/LIB/rand.r, and    the declaration of the post's own random() is left out.  - getlogin() is $USER, or `player' when that is unset.The module is named jumble2, the post's archive name: this disk's `jumble'is a different program, a solver that lists every ordering of a word.